when your cousin called.

238
00:12:37,966 --> 00:12:39,716
-I'm fine wherever.
-Okay, good, good.

239
00:12:39,717 --> 00:12:41,517
Because this bunk
is the one that's available.

240
00:12:43,054 --> 00:12:44,514
Boys, this is Fletch.

241
00:12:45,890 --> 00:12:47,330
Fill him in on what he missed, okay?

242
00:12:48,059 --> 00:12:49,352
All right.

243
00:12:53,815 --> 00:12:55,858
Is it true you came
in a cop car from jail?

244
00:12:57,485 --> 00:12:59,194
<i>♪ Fletch go fetch ♪</i>

245
00:12:59,195 --> 00:13:00,654
<i>♪ Fletch I bet you wanna play catch ♪</i>

246
00:13:00,655 --> 00:13:02,907
<i>♪ Fletcha, Fletch! Fletch, catch this! ♪</i>

247
00:13:05,493 --> 00:13:06,911
I'm Cliff.

248
00:13:16,629 --> 00:13:17,714
Relax.

249
00:13:19,007 --> 00:13:20,174
If I wanted to hurt you...

250
00:13:21,843 --> 00:13:23,011
I'd wait till lights out.

251
00:13:25,263 --> 00:13:28,598
<i>♪ One shot
This is the moment ♪</i>

252
00:13:28,599 --> 00:13:31,436
<i>♪ One chance
I'm gonna show them ♪</i>

253
00:13:31,978 --> 00:13:35,022
<i>♪ Dreams so close
I almost got it ♪</i>

254
00:13:35,023 --> 00:13:37,774
<i>♪ One beat away
And I'm ready to rock it ♪</i>

255
00:13:37,775 --> 00:13:39,694
-Yes! Sing it, girl!
-Oh.

256
00:13:40,194 --> 00:13:44,239
No, that wasn't singing,
that was, um, vowel support.

257
00:13:44,240 --> 00:13:47,452
A technical exercise
like scales or Pilates.

258
00:13:48,327 --> 00:13:49,745
It sounded like singing to me.

259
00:13:49,746 --> 00:13:53,290
Impossible. I come from a long line
of classical musicians.

260
00:13:53,291 --> 00:13:56,293
My parents forbid me from indulging in
recreational melody.

261
00:13:56,294 --> 00:13:57,295
It leads to...

262
00:13:57,962 --> 00:13:59,588
-jazz.
-Call it what you want,

263
00:13:59,589 --> 00:14:01,256
but it sounded good.

264
00:14:01,257 --> 00:14:04,551
And I look forward to competing against
your vocal Pilates.

265
00:14:04,552 --> 00:14:06,219
No, I am not competing.

266
00:14:06,220 --> 00:14:07,679
Um, I'm a cello player.

267
00:14:07,680 --> 00:14:10,515
I'm like the Wi-Fi,
essential but unnoticed.

268
00:14:10,516 --> 00:14:12,059
Well, log in, girl.

269
00:14:12,060 --> 00:14:14,187
I mean, I still plan on winning,

270
00:14:14,687 --> 00:14:17,481
but it's not a real competition without
some real competition.

271
00:14:17,482 --> 00:14:18,524
Me?

272
00:14:19,192 --> 00:14:20,234
Singing?

273
00:14:21,319 --> 00:14:24,321
I don't know. It just feels
so front and center.

274
00:14:24,322 --> 00:14:26,281
You know, with a cello,
you're the foundation,

275
00:14:26,282 --> 00:14:28,117
the candlestick supporting the flame.

276
00:14:28,785 --> 00:14:30,953
To actually be the flame?

277
00:14:33,498 --> 00:14:35,290
-I could never.
-I mean, you do you.

278
00:14:35,291 --> 00:14:37,418
But news flash, this is Camp Rock.

279
00:14:38,252 --> 00:14:40,421
Around here, even the candlesticks sing.

280
00:14:42,590 --> 00:14:46,176
<i>♪ We talk the talk
We're the kids of Camp Rock ♪</i>

281
00:14:46,177 --> 00:14:49,429
<i>♪ We walk the walk
We talk the talk ♪</i>

282
00:14:49,430 --> 00:14:52,057
<i>♪ We're the kids of Camp Rock ♪</i>

283
00:14:52,058 --> 00:14:53,935
Whoo!

284
00:14:59,398 --> 00:15:01,400
-You lose something?
-Yeah.

285
00:15:01,943 --> 00:15:03,819
Yeah. Uh... Uh... Uh...

286
00:15:03,820 --> 00:15:05,195
Drumsticks! The guys thought

287
00:15:05,196 --> 00:15:06,780
it'd be hilarious
to chuck 'em on the roof.

288
00:15:06,781 --> 00:15:09,367
Message received.

289
00:15:22,672 --> 00:15:23,755
Thanks.

290
00:15:23,756 --> 00:15:24,841
Yeah.

291
00:15:26,634 --> 00:15:29,928
<i>♪ Bounce to the beat
Bounce, bounce to the beat ♪</i>

292
00:15:29,929 --> 00:15:31,012
<i>♪ Bounce to the beat... ♪</i>

293
00:15:31,013 --> 00:15:33,932
Yo, that's been in my head
since breakfast. Do you ever get that?

294
00:15:33,933 --> 00:15:35,308
Yeah, actually, I do.

295
00:15:35,309 --> 00:15:38,145
Well, I'm gonna use it,
write the whole song,

296
00:15:38,146 --> 00:15:40,313
perform it, win, tour.

297
00:15:40,314 --> 00:15:41,315
Boom!

298
00:15:41,941 --> 00:15:43,024
New life.

299
00:15:43,025 --> 00:15:44,526
Good luck with that, buddy.

300
00:15:44,527 --> 00:15:45,819
Buddy?

301
00:15:45,820 --> 00:15:48,238
Should we harmonize later,
or is it too soon?

302
00:15:49,866 --> 00:15:51,366
Okay, so, you know that girl Rosie?

303
00:15:51,367 --> 00:15:53,326
The goddess with the cello?

304
00:15:53,327 --> 00:15:56,204
She says that for safety issues,
she avoids all cliffs.

305
00:15:56,205 --> 00:15:58,415
But that's just her way
of saying that she likes me.

306
00:15:58,416 --> 00:16:00,041
What's your take?

307
00:16:09,302 --> 00:16:10,552
Come in.

308
00:16:15,183 --> 00:16:16,975
-Hi. Rosie, right?
-Hi.

309
00:16:16,976 --> 00:16:20,396
Yes. I'd like to revise my workshop
registration, please.

310
00:16:21,522 --> 00:16:24,357
Let's see. "Hard Rock Basics,

311
00:16:24,358 --> 00:16:27,402
Songwriting, Center Stage 101."

312
00:16:27,403 --> 00:16:28,404
Wow.

313
00:16:29,530 --> 00:16:31,282
These are some adventurous choices.

314
00:16:32,909 --> 00:16:33,993
You go, girl.

315
00:16:35,244 --> 00:16:36,912
Consider your registration

316
00:16:36,913 --> 00:16:38,331
revised.

317
00:16:39,707 --> 00:16:41,124
Thank you very much.

318
00:16:45,087 --> 00:16:48,632
Callie, I'm so excited
for this competition.

319
00:16:48,633 --> 00:16:50,258
I have lots to do today.

320
00:16:50,259 --> 00:16:52,469
But I still can't believe
you're not competing.

321
00:16:52,470 --> 00:16:54,471
Look, I know my strengths.

322
00:16:54,472 --> 00:16:56,849
I could carry a tune but dance...

323
00:16:57,600 --> 00:16:59,351
that's my real voice.

324
00:16:59,352 --> 00:17:01,186
But Lark asked me to be her assistant.

325
00:17:01,187 --> 00:17:03,021
I mean, what's the first challenge?

326
00:17:03,022 --> 00:17:05,941
Sing Connect 3's biggest hit
and make it our own.

327
00:17:05,942 --> 00:17:08,318
We get to show Lark who we are as artists.

328
00:17:12,114 --> 00:17:14,115
Oh, practice rooms are open. Gotta go.

329
00:17:14,116 --> 00:17:15,576
Okay, you got this.

330
00:17:20,206 --> 00:17:22,165
Five, six, seven, eight.

331
00:17:22,166 --> 00:17:25,669
One, two, three, four,
and five, six, seven, eight,

332
00:17:25,670 --> 00:17:29,464
and one, two, three,
four, five, six, seven, eight, one...

333
00:17:29,465 --> 00:17:30,508
Hey.

334
00:17:32,468 --> 00:17:35,929
Not to be the practice room police,
but there's a 30-minute limit.

335
00:17:35,930 --> 00:17:37,556
Don't even worry about it, girl.

336
00:17:37,557 --> 00:17:38,765
Okay.

337
00:17:38,766 --> 00:17:44,688
Thing is, she's next for the room
and then he's next after that.

338
00:17:44,689 --> 00:17:48,817
So if I were you,
I'd try and find another room.

339
00:17:48,818 --> 00:17:52,988
But I love your whole vibe,
it's giving...

340
00:17:52,989 --> 00:17:54,155
effort.

341
00:17:56,367 --> 00:17:59,620
Again. Five, six, seven, eight.

342
00:18:09,297 --> 00:18:11,089
Hey, can I steal this room?

343
00:18:11,090 --> 00:18:12,173
All the others are taken.

344
00:18:12,174 --> 00:18:13,675
Hi, Sage. I'm doing good.

345
00:18:13,676 --> 00:18:14,843
How are you?

346
00:18:14,844 --> 00:18:17,846
Please, I really need it.

347
00:18:17,847 --> 00:18:19,557
Let me think about it for a second.

348
00:18:20,641 --> 00:18:22,143
-No.
-Desi.

349
00:18:22,727 --> 00:18:24,352
Come on, you're just messing around.

350
00:18:24,353 --> 00:18:25,687
I actually have to rehearse.

351
00:18:25,688 --> 00:18:26,980
The first challenge is tomorrow.

352
00:18:26,981 --> 00:18:28,440
And how do you know I'm not competing?

353
00:18:28,441 --> 00:18:30,150
Because every time I try
to get you to play

354
00:18:30,151 --> 00:18:32,527
Battle of the Bands,
you call me a sellout with no soul.

355
00:18:32,528 --> 00:18:34,280
Now, that does sound like me.

356
00:18:37,241 --> 00:18:38,242
All right.

357
00:18:38,993 --> 00:18:41,369
I'm pulling the big sister card. Out, now.

358
00:18:41,370 --> 00:18:44,623
Hey, if your fancy new music school
didn't prepare you for this competition,

359
00:18:44,624 --> 00:18:47,000
I don't know what half an hour
in a practice room is gonna do.

360
00:18:47,001 --> 00:18:49,085
You're still mad that I left the band
to go to Anthem.

361
00:18:49,086 --> 00:18:50,420
I don't know what you're talking about.

362
00:18:50,421 --> 00:18:52,548
I'm pretty sure
we sound better without you.

363
00:18:53,132 --> 00:18:57,093
I'm gonna be Connect 3's opening act,
and nothing's gonna throw me off my game.

364
00:18:57,094 --> 00:18:58,095
Not even you.

365
00:18:59,305 --> 00:19:00,722
Enjoy the room.

366
00:19:07,480 --> 00:19:09,230
<i>All competing campers,</i>

367
00:19:09,231 --> 00:19:11,816
<i>meet me in the dining hall
for the first challenge.</i>

368
00:19:11,817 --> 00:19:13,319
<i>Let's see who you are as an artist.</i>

369
00:19:13,944 --> 00:19:16,071
<i>I need vocals. I need star power.</i>

370
00:19:16,072 --> 00:19:17,322
<i>I need coffee.</i>

371
00:19:25,122 --> 00:19:26,123
Let's begin.

372
00:19:27,041 --> 00:19:28,333
Who's first?

373
00:19:28,334 --> 00:19:30,627
<i>♪ Turn on the radio ♪</i>

374
00:19:30,628 --> 00:19:33,380
<i>♪ As loud as it can go ♪</i>

375
00:19:33,381 --> 00:19:37,301
<i>♪ Wanna dance until
my feet can't feel the ground ♪</i>

376
00:19:38,678 --> 00:19:41,471
<i>♪ Say goodbye to all my fears ♪</i>

377
00:19:41,472 --> 00:19:44,349
<i>♪ One good song they disappear ♪</i>

378
00:19:44,350 --> 00:19:48,688
<i>♪ And nothing in the world
can bring me down ♪</i>

379
00:19:50,106 --> 00:19:52,399
<i>♪ Hand clapping earth-shaking ♪</i>

380
00:19:52,400 --> 00:19:54,818
<i>♪ Heartbreaking there's no... ♪</i>

381
00:19:54,819 --> 00:19:59,364
<i>♪ Faking what you feel
when you're right at home ♪</i>

382
00:19:59,365 --> 00:20:00,615
<i>♪ Yeah ♪</i>

383
00:20:00,616 --> 00:20:04,078
<i>♪ Music's in my soul ♪</i>

384
00:20:04,870 --> 00:20:09,082
<i>♪ I can hear it every day
and every night ♪</i>

385
00:20:09,083 --> 00:20:11,960
<i>♪ It's the one thing on my mind ♪</i>

386
00:20:11,961 --> 00:20:15,130
<i>♪ Music's got control ♪</i>

387
00:20:15,131 --> 00:20:18,049
<i>♪ And I'm never letting go ♪</i>

388
00:20:18,050 --> 00:20:19,592
<i>♪ No, no ♪</i>

389
00:20:19,593 --> 00:20:23,639
<i>♪ I just wanna play my music ♪</i>

390
00:20:24,807 --> 00:20:27,517
<i>♪ Got my six-string on my back ♪</i>

391
00:20:27,518 --> 00:20:30,895
<i>♪ Don't need anything but that ♪</i>

392
00:20:30,896 --> 00:20:35,859
<i>♪ Everything I want is here with me ♪</i>

393
00:20:35,860 --> 00:20:38,319
<i>♪ So forget that fancy car ♪</i>

394
00:20:38,320 --> 00:20:41,114
<i>♪ I don't need to go that far ♪</i>

395
00:20:41,115 --> 00:20:44,993
<i>♪ What's driving me
is following my dream ♪</i>

396
00:20:44,994 --> 00:20:47,036
<i>♪ Yeah ♪</i>

397
00:20:47,037 --> 00:20:49,414
<i>♪ Hand clapping earthshaking ♪</i>

398
00:20:49,415 --> 00:20:50,874
<i>♪ Heartbreaking ♪</i>

399
00:20:50,875 --> 00:20:53,418
<i>♪ There's no faking what you feel ♪</i>

400
00:20:53,419 --> 00:20:55,837
<i>♪ When you're on a roll ♪</i>

401
00:20:55,838 --> 00:20:57,547
<i>♪ Yeah ♪</i>

402
00:20:57,548 --> 00:21:01,342
<i>♪ Music's in my soul ♪</i>

403
00:21:01,343 --> 00:21:02,927
<i>♪ I can hear it ♪</i>

404
00:21:02,928 --> 00:21:05,722
<i>♪ Every day and every night ♪</i>

405
00:21:05,723 --> 00:21:08,433
<i>♪ It's the one thing on my mind ♪</i>

406
00:21:08,434 --> 00:21:11,729
<i>-♪ Music's got control ♪
-♪ Music's got control y'all ♪</i>

407
00:21:12,354 --> 00:21:14,064
<i>♪ Never let it go, no ♪</i>

408
00:21:14,857 --> 00:21:19,194
<i>♪ Oh no, no I just wanna
play my music ♪</i>

409
00:21:19,195 --> 00:21:22,822
<i>♪ Music's got control ♪</i>

410
00:21:22,823 --> 00:21:27,368
<i>♪ And I'm never letting go
No, no ♪</i>

411
00:21:27,369 --> 00:21:32,665
<i>♪ I just wanna play my music ♪</i>

412
00:21:32,666 --> 00:21:35,585
<i>♪ All night long ♪</i>

413
00:21:35,586 --> 00:21:36,629
<i>♪ Yeah ♪</i>

414
00:21:39,632 --> 00:21:43,051
Before I post the list
of campers moving on in the competition,

415
00:21:43,052 --> 00:21:46,095
I would just like to say, you are seen.

416
00:21:46,096 --> 00:21:47,430
You are enough.

417
00:21:47,431 --> 00:21:49,516
Please don't freak out, 'kay?

418
00:21:54,522 --> 00:21:56,481
Breathe, Luke, just think.

419
00:21:56,482 --> 00:21:59,484
You'll have front row seats
to someone else's dreams coming true.

420
00:22:01,362 --> 00:22:03,947
I mean, you'll get 'em next time.

421
00:22:08,869 --> 00:22:10,204
I'm so proud of you!

422
00:22:10,955 --> 00:22:12,122
Wait one sec.

423
00:22:14,124 --> 00:22:16,167
-Hi.
-Hey.

424
00:22:16,168 --> 00:22:18,003
I'm just gonna steal him for a sec.

425
00:22:21,799 --> 00:22:23,633
Desi, what are you doing here?

426
00:22:23,634 --> 00:22:25,927
What does it look like I'm doing?
I'm networking.

427
00:22:25,928 --> 00:22:27,470
You said you weren't even competing.

428
00:22:27,471 --> 00:22:29,389
Uh, I performed, didn't I?

429
00:22:29,390 --> 00:22:31,975
You crashed the auditions
in a hoodie with no plan.

430
00:22:31,976 --> 00:22:34,352
Sage, you were born planning things.

431
00:22:34,353 --> 00:22:36,312
I was born playing things.

432
00:22:36,313 --> 00:22:37,397
It's not a competition.

433
00:22:37,398 --> 00:22:39,148
This literally is a competition.

434
00:22:39,149 --> 00:22:41,360
I'll see you
at the next challenge, sis.

435
00:22:41,902 --> 00:22:43,278
Break a leg.

436
00:22:43,279 --> 00:22:44,697
Maybe even break two.

437
00:22:46,115 --> 00:22:47,199
For balance.

438
00:22:49,034 --> 00:22:50,411
Ugh.

439
00:22:54,415 --> 00:22:56,166
Hey, nice job back there.

440
00:22:56,667 --> 00:22:58,960
-Thanks.
-But kind of stiff.

441
00:23:00,045 --> 00:23:01,796
Loosen up and have fun with it.

442
00:23:01,797 --> 00:23:02,882
'Kay?

443
00:23:03,674 --> 00:23:04,758
'Kay.

444
00:23:11,974 --> 00:23:13,433
Hello down there.

445
00:23:13,434 --> 00:23:17,020
Any chance you guys could do me a solid
and go grab camp director, Connie?

446
00:23:17,021 --> 00:23:18,396
Funny story,

447
00:23:18,397 --> 00:23:20,273
I didn't think I was afraid of heights.

448
00:23:20,274 --> 00:23:22,026
Turns out I am.

449
00:23:25,154 --> 00:23:26,655
Appreciate you guys.

450
00:23:27,907 --> 00:23:29,825
You're gonna get her, right?

451
00:23:30,868 --> 00:23:33,745
Welcome to Camp Rock's
songwriting workshop.

452
00:23:33,746 --> 00:23:36,915
This isn't a part of the competition,
but I think it could really help.

453
00:23:36,916 --> 00:23:39,042
I have been wanting
to bring this next guy here

454
00:23:39,043 --> 00:23:40,627
for a while.

455
00:23:40,628 --> 00:23:43,046
He is an up-and-coming singer/songwriter

456
00:23:43,047 --> 00:23:46,467
and one of the most-streamed artists
of all last year.

457
00:23:47,092 --> 00:23:49,677
He's also one of my favorite
Camp Rock alums.

458
00:23:49,678 --> 00:23:50,887
Please welcome...

459
00:23:50,888 --> 00:23:53,056
Calvin Rhodes!

460
00:23:54,767 --> 00:23:56,059
Hi, Connie.

461
00:23:56,060 --> 00:23:57,560
Amazing.

462
00:23:57,561 --> 00:23:59,562
Welcome, future legends.

463
00:23:59,563 --> 00:24:01,064
I can't believe this is happening.

464
00:24:01,065 --> 00:24:02,523
His last album changed my life.

465
00:24:02,524 --> 00:24:04,901
Songwriting is all in the details, okay?

466
00:24:04,902 --> 00:24:07,028
It's about the feeling under the feeling.

467
00:24:07,029 --> 00:24:08,488
Don't tell me that she smiled.

468
00:24:08,489 --> 00:24:12,576
Tell me that her smile
holds the promise of a thousand dreams.

469
00:24:15,829 --> 00:24:17,038
Let's start smaller. Okay.

470
00:24:17,039 --> 00:24:18,957
Let's pair up
and let's interview each other.

471
00:24:18,958 --> 00:24:21,793
No. No, no, no, no, no.
Don't think you're getting off that easy.

472
00:24:21,794 --> 00:24:24,796
I want you to interview
a camper that you haven't met before.

473
00:24:24,797 --> 00:24:27,632
Now, really ask
the weird questions, dig deep,

474
00:24:27,633 --> 00:24:29,009
find out what makes them tick.

475
00:24:29,593 --> 00:24:31,052
Turn to the camper behind you.

476
00:24:31,053 --> 00:24:33,013
Back row. Turn to the camper
on your right.

477
00:24:39,269 --> 00:24:41,313
-Hey.
-Hey.

478
00:24:42,648 --> 00:24:45,442
Five, six, seven, turn.

479
00:24:47,069 --> 00:24:48,153
Eight.

480
00:24:48,654 --> 00:24:50,489
Hey, Desi, no songwriting for you?

481
00:24:51,073 --> 00:24:52,574
No. Workshops aren't for me.

482
00:24:53,784 --> 00:24:55,118
You want to be a stand-in?

483
00:24:55,119 --> 00:24:56,953
I need help figuring out this transition.

484
00:24:56,954 --> 00:24:59,122
Pass, I am not a dancer.

485
00:24:59,123 --> 00:25:01,833
Well, if you want to open for Connect 3,
you kinda have to dance.

486
00:25:01,834 --> 00:25:03,793
Nah, I'll stick with what I know.

487
