I can't.

733
00:38:13,500 --> 00:38:16,251
I never thought Maddie the Baddie
would go down in a dance challenge.

734
00:38:16,252 --> 00:38:18,670
And yet, balance is restored!

735
00:38:20,298 --> 00:38:21,633
Speaking of baddies...

736
00:38:22,133 --> 00:38:23,801
Callie, don't even...

737
00:38:23,802 --> 00:38:25,427
Okay, look, I'm not saying
your brother is cute.

738
00:38:25,428 --> 00:38:28,347
I'm just saying he's not, not cute.

739
00:38:28,348 --> 00:38:30,140
Absolutely not.

740
00:38:30,141 --> 00:38:31,226
Stop.

741
00:38:32,101 --> 00:38:33,477
Sorry, we're closed.

742
00:38:33,478 --> 00:38:34,838
I actually came to talk to Callie.

743
00:38:36,314 --> 00:38:37,606
Go ahead.

744
00:38:37,607 --> 00:38:38,816
Alone.

745
00:38:38,817 --> 00:38:39,901
Okay.

746
00:38:46,825 --> 00:38:49,034
You're a really good dancer.

747
00:38:49,035 --> 00:38:50,787
Agreed. Thank you.

748
00:38:51,538 --> 00:38:53,205
Me not so much.

749
00:38:53,206 --> 00:38:55,582
I was thinking
maybe you could help me out.

750
00:38:55,583 --> 00:38:58,961
Give me a few... lessons.

751
00:38:58,962 --> 00:39:01,380
Wait, you want me to do what?

752
00:39:01,381 --> 00:39:02,923
Please don't make me say it again.

753
00:39:02,924 --> 00:39:04,132
So you're actually gonna compete?

754
00:39:04,133 --> 00:39:05,384
Baby steps, Callie.

755
00:39:05,385 --> 00:39:07,803
First, you gotta teach me how to dance.

756
00:39:07,804 --> 00:39:10,139
Okay. But I'm not gonna go easy on you.

757
00:39:10,932 --> 00:39:11,933
So get ready.

758
00:39:12,642 --> 00:39:13,726
Cooler by the fire pit.

759
00:39:15,812 --> 00:39:18,605
Come on! Don't eat all
the marshmallows, people.

760
00:39:18,606 --> 00:39:20,274
Save it for tonight.

761
00:39:20,275 --> 00:39:22,318
Why is it so hard?

762
00:39:24,404 --> 00:39:26,071
Hey, Nate. What's going on?

763
00:39:26,072 --> 00:39:28,156
Hey, Lark. Can you tell Shane
that the suits are happening.

764
00:39:28,157 --> 00:39:29,241
<i>He listens to you.</i>

765
00:39:29,242 --> 00:39:30,367
Hang on.

766
00:39:30,368 --> 00:39:31,451
Hey, Shane.

767
00:39:31,452 --> 00:39:33,287
Can you tell Nate
we're not dressing up as groomsmen.

768
00:39:33,288 --> 00:39:35,247
You guys know you can say this
to each other directly.

769
00:39:35,248 --> 00:39:37,124
<i>We tried. It got loud.</i>

770
00:39:37,125 --> 00:39:39,001
Hang on!

771
00:39:39,002 --> 00:39:41,128
Jason, please tell me
this is not about wardrobe.

772
00:39:41,129 --> 00:39:42,379
-No.
-Fantastic.

773
00:39:42,380 --> 00:39:44,132
-Have you seen my child?
-Jason!

774
00:39:44,674 --> 00:39:47,259
You know what?
I have had enough of you three.

775
00:39:47,260 --> 00:39:49,887
Gentlemen, this is not
a conference call I asked for.

776
00:39:49,888 --> 00:39:51,889
<i>You are grown men. Use your words</i>

777
00:39:51,890 --> 00:39:52,973
with each other.

778
00:39:52,974 --> 00:39:54,808
I just want us to look like
we belong up there.

779
00:39:54,809 --> 00:39:56,226
And I just want us to feel like us,

780
00:39:56,227 --> 00:39:58,604
-not the version everyone expects.
-<i>Figure it out, guys!</i>

781
00:39:58,605 --> 00:40:00,856
I'm about to produce
a bonfire for the first time.

782
00:40:00,857 --> 00:40:02,733
And yes, there is a learning curve.

783
00:40:02,734 --> 00:40:03,942
I'm hanging up.

784
00:40:03,943 --> 00:40:05,027
Wait, wait, wait.
How's the competition going?

785
00:40:05,028 --> 00:40:06,111
<i>Great.</i>

786
00:40:06,112 --> 00:40:07,404
<i>We're down to our final five.</i>

787
00:40:07,405 --> 00:40:09,615
We just need to make sure they can really
handle being on tour.

788
00:40:09,616 --> 00:40:13,327
Exactly. A successful tour is about
more than just talent.

789
00:40:13,328 --> 00:40:14,661
<i>Yeah. Long nights,</i>

790
00:40:14,662 --> 00:40:17,998
tight spaces, terrible food.
They gotta be able to survive the grind.

791
00:40:17,999 --> 00:40:19,207
And if they can handle that,

792
00:40:19,208 --> 00:40:20,792
they can pretty much handle
being on the road.

793
00:40:20,793 --> 00:40:23,170
Hmm. No, not again.

794
00:40:23,171 --> 00:40:24,296
Oh, uh, update,

795
00:40:24,297 --> 00:40:26,340
-I found the baby.
-Great.

796
00:40:26,341 --> 00:40:27,799
You know what? I gotta go.

797
00:40:27,800 --> 00:40:31,012
Canela. No, Emmy, drop the marshmallows!

798
00:40:31,804 --> 00:40:34,515
<i>♪ Most days I am inspired ♪</i>

799
00:40:35,600 --> 00:40:38,226
<i>♪ Some days I am awake ♪</i>

800
00:40:39,479 --> 00:40:44,983
<i>♪ I'm confident and insecure
even at my best ♪</i>

801
00:40:44,984 --> 00:40:46,234
Not bad.

802
00:40:46,235 --> 00:40:47,987
I'm still struggling with the lyrics.

803
00:40:49,322 --> 00:40:50,865
You just gotta have fun with it.

804
00:40:51,908 --> 00:40:53,743
You make it sound so easy.

805
00:40:59,040 --> 00:41:03,877
All right, just so you know,
all of this isn't gonna distract me.

806
00:41:03,878 --> 00:41:06,047
-All right? I'm in it to win it.
-So am I.

807
00:41:09,717 --> 00:41:11,551
Can I ask you something?

808
00:41:11,552 --> 00:41:13,220
What's with you and your brother?

809
00:41:15,264 --> 00:41:16,431
You picked up on that?

810
00:41:16,432 --> 00:41:18,184
Yeah, it's kinda hard not to.

811
00:41:18,977 --> 00:41:20,603
We used to be in a band together,

812
00:41:21,688 --> 00:41:23,064
and then I left for Anthem.

813
00:41:24,357 --> 00:41:26,234
I wanted to take my music seriously.

814
00:41:27,068 --> 00:41:29,946
When the band broke up,
it kind of felt like we did, too.

815
00:41:34,826 --> 00:41:36,326
Can I ask you something?

816
00:41:36,327 --> 00:41:37,786
If you must.

817
00:41:37,787 --> 00:41:39,788
Are you really the bad boy
everyone says you are?

818
00:41:39,789 --> 00:41:41,039
Define bad.

819
00:41:41,040 --> 00:41:43,125
You showed up to camp in a cop car.

820
00:41:50,133 --> 00:41:54,971
Um, truth is, I came straight from court.

821
00:41:56,931 --> 00:42:01,810
My mom passed away in March,
and it was always just me and her,

822
00:42:01,811 --> 00:42:03,604
and now it's just me.

823
00:42:05,440 --> 00:42:07,040
A judge is figuring out where I go next.

824
00:42:08,693 --> 00:42:10,111
Fletch, I'm so sorry.

825
00:42:11,946 --> 00:42:13,531
But I'm really glad you're here.

826
00:42:17,660 --> 00:42:20,203
<i>♪ Sage and Fletch
sitting in a... ♪</i>

827
00:42:20,204 --> 00:42:21,663
Shoot!

828
00:42:21,664 --> 00:42:23,207
Guys, a little help?

829
00:42:24,584 --> 00:42:26,169
-You hungry?
-Starving.

830
00:42:26,794 --> 00:42:28,670
Come on. How am I supposed
to get back to shore?

831
00:42:28,671 --> 00:42:30,005
I can't swim.

832
00:42:30,006 --> 00:42:31,339
Yeah, you can, Cliff.

833
00:42:31,340 --> 00:42:33,217
I know I can. But I don't want to.

834
00:42:37,096 --> 00:42:38,513
-Stay vigilant.
-Mmm.

835
00:42:38,514 --> 00:42:40,015
Revenge is near.

836
00:42:42,810 --> 00:42:44,770
-Oh.
-It's a zombie. I still need to glaze it.

837
00:42:44,771 --> 00:42:46,021
Impressive.

838
00:42:47,732 --> 00:42:49,859
Maddie, can we go over the plan again?

839
00:42:50,443 --> 00:42:53,905
They each got the message
that Lark wanted a style consult.

840
00:42:54,864 --> 00:42:56,198
They'll be here any minute.

841
00:42:56,199 --> 00:42:58,867
-Wait, are you sure we shou...
-Don't gaslight me, Daniel.

842
00:42:58,868 --> 00:43:00,410
Mmm.

843
00:43:00,411 --> 00:43:03,289
They sabotaged us in the dance challenge.

844
00:43:04,040 --> 00:43:05,290
We are not the problem here.

845
00:43:05,291 --> 00:43:06,583
-Mmm-mmm.
-They are.

846
00:43:06,584 --> 00:43:10,630
We bring joy to millions
with our joyful content that promotes joy.

847
00:43:11,255 --> 00:43:13,673
But somehow those five
are the chosen ones?

848
00:43:13,674 --> 00:43:14,842
I don't think so.

849
00:43:20,681 --> 00:43:22,474
What are you guys doing here?

850
00:43:22,475 --> 00:43:24,101
Welcome to your style consult.

851
00:43:24,102 --> 00:43:26,561
Lark didn't call you here. We did.

852
00:43:26,562 --> 00:43:28,814
We thought you all needed
more elevated looks, you know,

853
00:43:28,815 --> 00:43:30,733
so your performances will really pop.

854
00:43:32,443 --> 00:43:35,153
All of you needed serious redesigning.

855
00:43:35,154 --> 00:43:36,488
Desi,

856
00:43:36,489 --> 00:43:39,491
you'll never have what it takes
to shine on stage.

857
00:43:39,492 --> 00:43:41,577
But, hey, at least your sneakers will.

858
00:43:43,913 --> 00:43:45,163
Fletch.

859
00:43:45,164 --> 00:43:47,917
Some preschool realness
for our mysterious musician.

860
00:43:49,377 --> 00:43:51,128
-Cliff.
-My drumsticks!

861
00:43:51,129 --> 00:43:52,505
Now, they're as weird as you are.

862
00:43:55,842 --> 00:43:57,759
Fix your branding problem, Sage.

863
00:43:57,760 --> 00:43:59,761
This is next level petty, Madison!

864
00:43:59,762 --> 00:44:01,848
Whatever major loser!

865
00:44:02,348 --> 00:44:07,019
And you know, Rosie,
classical music is just so stuffy.

866
00:44:07,770 --> 00:44:09,397
I thought I'd help you with that.

867
00:44:11,232 --> 00:44:13,066
You bedazzled my cello!

868
00:44:13,067 --> 00:44:15,735
Watch out! Metronome Mary is angry.

869
00:44:18,114 --> 00:44:20,157
Nobody talks to Rosie like that!

870
00:44:20,158 --> 00:44:21,533
Cliff!

871
00:44:21,534 --> 00:44:24,452
<i>♪ I hope you're ready
for the time of your life ♪</i>

872
00:44:24,453 --> 00:44:26,213
<i>♪ Just look at me
I put a gleam in your eye ♪</i>

873
00:44:27,248 --> 00:44:28,331
<i>♪ Buckle up ♪</i>

874
00:44:29,417 --> 00:44:30,625
<i>♪ We're gonna take you for a ride ♪</i>

875
00:44:30,626 --> 00:44:32,627
Okay, now, it's on!

876
00:44:33,838 --> 00:44:37,174
<i>♪ Let's go, we gotcha goin'
get in the vibe ♪</i>

877
00:44:37,175 --> 00:44:40,093
<i>-♪ Everybody put your hands to the sky ♪</i>
-Cliff!

878
00:44:41,179 --> 00:44:44,347
<i>♪ Buckle up, we're gonna
take you, take you high ♪</i>

879
00:44:44,348 --> 00:44:46,224
<i>-♪ Ah-ooh ♪</i>
-Nice, Rosie!

880
00:44:46,225 --> 00:44:48,226
<i>♪ Show me, show me show me... ♪</i>

881
00:44:48,227 --> 00:44:49,644
Desi, help me.

882
00:44:49,645 --> 00:44:52,856
<i>♪ C'mon, c'mon, c'mon,
c'mon, ready or not ♪</i>

883
00:44:52,857 --> 00:44:55,859
<i>♪ La-la-la-la-la-la
let me see how you vibe ♪</i>

884
00:44:55,860 --> 00:44:58,529
<i>-♪ It's on, it's on, it's on ♪</i>
-Go, Rosie!

885
00:44:59,322 --> 00:45:01,698
<i>♪ Get crazy, crazy, crazy
take it over the top ♪</i>

886
00:45:01,699 --> 00:45:04,284
I gotta admit, Fletch,
I'm a bit disappointed.

887
00:45:04,285 --> 00:45:06,245
I expected more from a guy
with your reputation.

888
00:45:06,829 --> 00:45:08,581
You know nothing about me, Madison.

889
00:45:10,625 --> 00:45:12,167
<i>-♪ Okay, now ♪</i>
-Watch out!

890
00:45:12,168 --> 00:45:13,376
<i>♪ Are you ready? ♪</i>

891
00:45:13,377 --> 00:45:14,544
No!

892
00:45:14,545 --> 00:45:17,255
<i>♪ One, two
One, two, three, four! ♪</i>

893
00:45:17,256 --> 00:45:19,342
Guys, we gotta go now!

894
00:45:19,926 --> 00:45:21,009
<i>♪ 'Cause we, 'cause we ♪</i>

895
00:45:21,010 --> 00:45:23,011
<i>♪ 'Cause when we rock we let it rock ♪</i>

896
00:45:23,012 --> 00:45:24,179
<i>♪ Rock it, rock it rock it ♪</i>

897
00:45:24,180 --> 00:45:25,680
<i>♪ Rock it, dance till we drop ♪</i>

898
00:45:25,681 --> 00:45:28,517
Um, guys?

899
00:45:31,145 --> 00:45:32,395
<i>♪ It's on! ♪</i>

900
00:45:34,523 --> 00:45:36,316
<i>So, Connie spoke
to Madison's parents.</i>

901
00:45:36,317 --> 00:45:38,693
They'll be replacing
everything she trashed,

902
00:45:38,694 --> 00:45:41,279
including your cello,
instead of buying her a car.

903
00:45:41,280 --> 00:45:43,073
Justice! Sweet justice.

904
00:45:43,074 --> 00:45:45,283
Uh-uh. Don't pat yourselves on the back.

905
00:45:45,284 --> 00:45:48,495
You five weren't exactly
innocent bystanders, you were part of it.

906
00:45:48,496 --> 00:45:50,497
It's like a glitter apocalypse.

907
00:45:50,498 --> 00:45:53,041
Okay. Well, you saw what they did to
our stuff though, right?

908
00:45:53,042 --> 00:45:54,292
We were just defending ourselves.

909
00:45:54,293 --> 00:45:55,961
Yeah, my cello was vandalized.

910
00:45:55,962 --> 00:45:57,379
I was simply avenging its honor.

911
00:45:57,380 --> 00:45:59,464
I hear you, but it really doesn't matter.

912
00:45:59,465 --> 00:46:01,591
This behavior is unacceptable on tour.

913
00:46:01,592 --> 00:46:03,343
Okay, well, I didn't start it.

914
00:46:03,344 --> 00:46:05,262
I was just avenging your honor.

915
00:46:05,263 --> 00:46:07,097
Thank you, but I didn't ask you to.

916
00:46:07,098 --> 00:46:08,765
Sage was the one who told me
to grab the paint.

917
00:46:08,766 --> 00:46:10,600
Oh, so now you start listening to me?

918
00:46:10,601 --> 00:46:12,978
Yeah, and at the end,
I was just defending Fletch.

919
00:46:12,979 --> 00:46:15,188
-I can handle myself, okay?
-Yeah, but we're buddy.

920
00:46:17,066 --> 00:46:18,150
Enough!

921
00:46:19,318 --> 00:46:22,612
If you can't handle each other,
in an arts and crafts room,

922
00:46:22,613 --> 00:46:24,282
how do you expect to survive here?

923
00:46:30,830 --> 00:46:33,416
Welcome to your third and final challenge.

924
00:46:35,001 --> 00:46:36,127
The camp bus?

925
00:46:45,052 --> 00:46:46,387
We must get rid of them.

926
00:46:47,138 --> 00:46:48,723
And I know exactly how to do it.

927
00:46:49,473 --> 00:46:52,392
Lark is not gonna be happy when she finds
a video of the third challenge

928
00:46:52,393 --> 00:46:53,644
posted by the final five.

929
00:46:54,812 --> 00:46:57,272
That'll ruin the whole competition.

930
00:46:57,273 --> 00:46:58,732
What a shame!

931
00:46:58,733 --> 00:47:00,567
But they wouldn't post a video.

932
00:47:00,568 --> 00:47:01,901
They'd be disqualified.

933
00:47:01,902 --> 00:47:04,070
-I'm posting the video, Daniel.
-Oh!

934
00:47:04,071 --> 00:47:07,615
Now, go sneak into Connie's office
and get my phone.

935
00:47:07,616 --> 00:47:09,618
- On it. Let's go, Danielle
- Ugh.

936
00:47:10,870 --> 00:47:13,830
Here it is! Your home
for the next 24 hours.

937
00:47:13,831 --> 00:47:15,165
Twenty-four hours?

938
00:47:15,166 --> 00:47:16,806
-So we have to sleep on this bus?
-Yep.

939
00:47:17,460 --> 00:47:20,420
But Final Jam's in two days.
I've got stuff to do.

940
00:47:20,421 --> 00:47:23,715
Prep here then. Because this is about
more than just music.

941
00:47:23,716 --> 00:47:26,259
It's about proving
you can handle tour life.

942
00:47:26,260 --> 00:47:27,886
The challenge is just to sit here?

943
00:47:27,887 --> 00:47:29,846
Not just sit, stay.

944
00:47:29,847 --> 00:47:32,724
If anyone steps off this bus,
you're eliminated!

945
00:47:34,560 --> 00:47:36,187
Is there even a bathroom on here?

946
00:47:38,230 --> 00:47:40,065
Ta da!

947
00:47:40,066 --> 00:47:41,232
Oh come on!

948
00:47:41,233 --> 00:47:43,777
A porta-potty in the summer
is basically a poop oven.

949
00:47:43,778 --> 00:47:45,695
So you have been to Coachella.

950
00:47:45,696 --> 00:47:48,490
I can't. Porta-potties are my nightmare.

951
00:47:48,491 --> 00:47:51,493
Yeah. She got locked inside one
at a soccer field for like an hour.

952
00:47:51,494 --> 00:47:53,912
Yeah, because you told Dad
I was at a playdate.

953
00:47:53,913 --> 00:47:55,872
Technically, you were.
Just you and the toilet though.

954
00:47:55,873 --> 00:47:57,290
Okay, we're done here.

955
00:47:57,291 --> 00:48:00,293
FYI, this is what touring feels like.

956
00:48:00,294 --> 00:48:04,756
No privacy, tight spaces,
annoying people breathing your air.

957
00:48:04,757 --> 00:48:08,636
If you want to survive out there,
learn to survive in here.

958
00:48:39,333 --> 00:48:40,418
Cliff...

959
00:48:41,544 --> 00:48:42,628
It's time.

960
00:48:43,504 --> 00:48:46,047
Don't let anyone open it.
And make sure nobody knocks it over.

961
00:48:46,048 --> 00:48:47,633
Roger that. You can count on me.

962
00:48:49,510 --> 00:48:50,511
Okay.

963
00:49:02,898 --> 00:49:04,108
Come on.

964
00:49:13,701 --> 00:49:16,411
Were you able to secure the contraband
from Connie's office?

965
00:49:16,412 --> 00:49:18,037
I have no idea what that means.

966
00:49:18,038 --> 00:49:20,665
Yeah. Wait, why are we doing this again?

967
00:49:20,666 --> 00:49:21,792
Because, Daniel,

968
00:49:22,835 --> 00:49:24,879
sometimes karma needs a little push.

969
00:49:25,838 --> 00:49:27,547
I want them disqualified.

970
00:49:27,548 --> 00:49:28,798
Oh, wow.

971
00:49:28,799 --> 00:49:30,550
-You really hate them.
-I don't

972
00:49:30,551 --> 00:49:32,135
use the word hate, Danielle?

973
00:49:33,679 --> 00:49:36,474
I simply release people
who no longer serve my journey.

974
00:49:37,349 --> 00:49:39,185
I release them really hard.

975
00:49:40,895 --> 00:49:43,396
Calm down, Danielle.

976
00:49:43,397 --> 00:49:44,482
Can you not...

977
00:49:57,828 --> 00:50:00,664
How can he sleep so well in here?

978
00:50:17,556 --> 00:50:19,140
I had the most horrible dream, guys.

979
